{"The type check isinstance(process, multiprocessing.Process) may not match multiprocessing.context.SpawnProcess, so kill()/terminate() paths might not run as intended. Should check against multiprocessing.context.BaseProcess or use duck-typing on terminate/kill.": 0.2938610315322876, "When max_processes is 0 or when there are 0 assigned_shards, num_processes can become 0 and the modulo-based shard distribution will crash with division by zero. Need to validate max_processes (>=1) and short-circuit when there are no shards, or fall back to 1 process.": 0.7354696393013, "Restart logic creates a new process/thread but does not clearly stop/join the previous one before replacing it, which can lead to leaked threads/processes and duplicated flushers running concurrently. The previous worker should be reliably terminated/joined before respawn.": 0.5950011014938354, "Per-worker resources (e.g., producer) are not deterministically stored/closed during process restart.": 0.239402636885643}